    "passage": "Meera and Dan were helping their class make a huge picture of a park. Meera carefully drew flowers in one corner while Dan painted a path. When their teacher asked whether they were finished, Meera shook her head. She could still see places where more flowers might fit. Dan had already put his brush down, but he waited beside her. He asked where someone in the picture would walk to reach the flowers. Meera looked at the path and noticed it stopped before her corner. She put down her flower pencil and helped him extend the path. Now it curved around the flowers and joined the rest of the park. Meera stepped back far enough to see the whole picture. She decided that her corner did not need another flower. It had needed a way for the rest of the picture to reach it.",
